NAME
    kill - cancel a job, remove a breakpoint or watch, or kill a session

SYNOPSIS
    kill <id>

DESCRIPTION
    Terminates or removes an active entry shown by ps(1) using its id.
    kill routes <id> to the module claiming its prefix (case-insensitive)
    before falling back to session names:

    bp<N>       Remove breakpoint N (emusen.trace).
    watch<N>    Remove watch N (emusen.trace).
    chd<N>      Cancel background CHD job N (emusen.library).
    pkg<N>      Cancel background package job N (emusen.library).
    rom<N>      Cancel background ROM job N (emusen.library).
    cores<N>    Cancel background core job N (emusen.cores).
    scrape<N>   Cancel background scrape job N (emusen.scrape).
    <session>   Destroy named tmux(1) session.

    Killing a session follows the same rules as 'tmux kill': the last
    remaining session cannot be killed, and killing the active session
    switches to a remaining one. If a session's name collides with a
    claimed job prefix, use 'tmux kill <name>' directly.

EXAMPLES
    kill bp1
    kill watch3
    kill scrape1
    kill investigation

EXIT STATUS
    0   Target job, breakpoint, watch, or session was removed.
    1   Missing id, unknown id, no session manager, or refusal to kill
        the last remaining session.

SEE ALSO
    ps(1), tmux(1), bp(1), watch(1)
